From: Iltix <dev@iltix.de>
Date: Sat, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:05 +0000
Subject: Iltix Module Hooks — wire Theme, Navigation and AutoHide into Chromium

Adds the minimal call-sites that activate Iltix modules inside existing
Chromium/Cromite source files. All calls are guarded by IltixModuleManager
and are no-ops when the respective module is disabled.

Changes (minimal upstream footprint):

1. ChromeBrowserInitializer — init IltixModuleManager early in pre-native
   startup so all subsequent module checks work without null-pointer risk.
   Hook pattern matches existing ChromeSharedPreferences.warmUp() call from
   Add-option-to-force-tablet-UI.patch.

2. ChromeTabbedActivity — call IltixThemeModule.applyWindowTheme() at the
   start of onCreate, before the super call, so window flags are set before
   the first view is measured.
   Hook pattern matches existing ApplicationLifetime import from
   Add-exit-menu-item.patch.

3. BottomControlsCoordinator — after the bottom toolbar view is fully
   constructed, wire up IltixNavBarCoordinator (Navigation module) and
   IltixThemeModule.applyNavBarGlass() (Theme module) on the container.

4. BottomControlsMediator — store the auto-hide controller reference and
   forward the topOffset scroll delta to IltixAutoHideController when
   the AutoHide module is enabled.

Total upstream lines added: ~8 additions across 4 files.
All new class references are in org.chromium.chrome.browser.iltix.*

Requires: Iltix-Module-Settings-Infrastructure.patch
Requires: Iltix-Module-Theme.patch
Requires: Iltix-Module-Navigation.patch
Requires: Iltix-Module-AutoHideNavigation.patch

